;;; The twin of `wild-in-head.ein`: the same program with the head
;;; wildcard written out as the disjunction over the relations it has that a
;;; one-argument fact can belong to, `holds` and `hit`. A fresh variable is
;;; no twin for a head (a relation head is bound by the activator, Q29). `w`
;;; fires on `(holds a)`, root holds `(hit w)`, and R is `{(hit w)}` and
;;; `{(hit a), (hit w)}` (`ein solve FILE`). The witness's right answer is
;;; its refusal (Q-M1e2.22); this is the answer of the program written out,
;;; which loads.
;;;
;;;

(relation holds Node :why "{?1} holds") (relation hit Node :why "{?1} is hit")
(holds a)
(rule w () :match (or (holds a) (hit a)) :assert (hit w) :why "a holds or a is hit, so w is hit")
